Docker Registry

1) Image Tag
ex : docker run postgres:10.10
    here, whaterver value after : is the version of the Image
    If we didnt specify, it will take latest by default

2) Docker Registry - Pushing Images

- You can have your Private or Public Repo

3) Docker Image Naming Convention

- syntax : registry/username_or_org/repository:tag
    registry - (Optional) domain of the container registry - default to docker.io
    username_or_org - name of user or org(required for non-official images only)
    repository - the name of the image or the project

4) Rename Image

- used to add a new name (or alias) to an existing Docker Image 
- syntax : docker tag SOURCE_IMAGE[:TAG] TARGET_IMAGE[:TAG]
- ex : docker tag python:3.10 my-python-app:latest


for docker registry
- Syntax : docker tag SOURCE_IMAGE REGESTRY_HOST/USERNAME/REPO:TAG
- ex : docker tag myapp registry.mycorp.com/devops/myapp:1.0.0

5) Docker Registry - Login Command
- you have to login to the docker hub to push the image to repo
- syntax : docker login registry_host

For dockerHub , you do not need to specify the registry as it default to docker.io

- syntax : docker tag LOCAL_IMAGE_NAME:TAG USERNAME/REPO:TAG

6) Docker Registry - docker push command 
- docker push uploads a locally tag resource to the docker registry (like docker hub, Github container registry, AWS ECR)

- Syntax : docker push [REGISTRY_HOST]/USERNAME/REPO:TAG

for docker : docker push myapp myusername/myapp:latest
for generic registry : docker push registry.mycorp.com/devops/myapp:10.0.0

